11
01:09:18,000 --> 01:09:24,000
The Mist is a 2007 American horror film produced,
written, and directed by Frank Darabont.

12
01:15:36,000 --> 01:15:42,000
Based on Stephen King's  1980 novella, the film stars an ensemble cast including Thomas
Jane, Marcia Gay Harden, Laurie Holden, Andre Braugher and Toby Jones.

13
01:21:54,000 --> 01:22:00,000
The plot follows a group of people in the small town of Bridgton, Maine, who become trapped inside a
supermarket after a mysterious mist envelops the town, concealing deadly, Lovecraftian creatures.

14
01:28:12,000 --> 01:28:18,000
As fear and paranoia spread, tensions rise among the survivors.

15
01:34:30,000 --> 01:34:36,000
While the film is primarily a monster movie, it explores how
ordinary people react under extreme circumstances.

16
01:40:48,000 --> 01:40:54,000
Darabont notably altered the novella's ending, a change that King praised stating that people who spoil the ending should be “hung by the neck until dead.”
The Mist was filmed in Shreveport, Louisiana, beginning in February 2007,
premiered at ShowEast on October 18, 2007, and was released in the United States on November 21, 2007, by Dimension Films (through Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer), with The Weinstein Company distributing in international markets.

17
01:47:06,000 --> 01:47:12,000
The film received generally positive reviews from critics, and
grossed $57.5 million on a $13–18 million budget.

18
01:53:24,000 --> 01:53:30,000
The film explores themes of monster, based on novel
or book, supermarket, fight, faith.

